Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• PUBLICATIONS."cpc": CPC classification codes; filter rows whose codes start with ‘A61%’.  
• PUBLICATIONS."assignee_harmonized": nested JSON/VARIANT that holds the harmonized assignee name(s); used to identify / group patents by assignee.  
• PUBLICATIONS."publication_date": numeric YYYYMMDD; extract the first four digits to build the “year” for “busiest year” checks.  
• PUBLICATIONS."country_code": two‑letter patent‑office / jurisdiction code; count where the top assignee files the most patents.  
• PUBLICATIONS."publication_number": handy identifier when previewing sample rows.  
Possible conditions that may be applied later  
• LATERAL FLATTEN on "cpc" and on "assignee_harmonized" to get individual codes / names.  
• WHERE cpc_symbol ILIKE 'A61%' to keep only A61 category.  
• WHERE assignee_name ILIKE '%Target Assignee%' for assignee filtering once found.  
• WHERE TO_CHAR("publication_date") LIKE 'YYYY%'  (or substr / integer math) for year constraints.  

Ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows)  
```sql
--Description: 1‑Quick peek at the raw CPC JSON structure.
SELECT 
    "publication_number",
    "cpc"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2‑Flatten CPC and list distinct CPC symbols (first 20) to see how “A61” looks.
SELECT DISTINCT 
       f.value:"symbol"::STRING AS cpc_symbol
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") f
WHERE f.value IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3‑Show sample rows whose CPC symbol starts with 'A61'.
SELECT 
    p."publication_number",
    f.value:"symbol"::STRING AS cpc_symbol
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") f
WHERE f.value:"symbol"::STRING ILIKE 'A61%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4‑Inspect the structure of the harmonized assignee field.
SELECT 
    "publication_number",
    "assignee_harmonized"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5‑Flatten harmonized assignee list and list the first 20 distinct names.
SELECT DISTINCT 
       a.value:"name"::STRING AS assignee_name
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."assignee_harmonized") a
WHERE a.value IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6‑Count A61‑category publications by assignee (top 20 assignees).
SELECT 
       a.value:"name"::STRING          AS assignee_name,
       COUNT(DISTINCT p."publication_number") AS patent_cnt
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc")      c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."assignee_harmonized") a
WHERE c.value:"symbol"::STRING ILIKE 'A61%'
GROUP BY assignee_name
ORDER BY patent_cnt DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7‑Annual counts for the single most‑active assignee in A61 (replace ***TopName*** later).
SELECT 
       SUBSTR(CAST(p."publication_date" AS STRING),1,4) AS pub_year,
       COUNT(DISTINCT p."publication_number")          AS patents_in_year
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc")      c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."assignee_harmonized") a
WHERE c.value:"symbol"::STRING ILIKE 'A61%'
  AND a.value:"name"::STRING = '***TopName***'
GROUP BY pub_year
ORDER BY patents_in_year DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8‑Jurisdiction counts during busiest year for that assignee (replace ***TopName*** and ***BusiestYear***).
SELECT 
       p."country_code",
       COUNT(DISTINCT p."publication_number") AS patents_in_year_country
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc")      c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."assignee_harmonized") a
WHERE c.value:"symbol"::STRING ILIKE 'A61%'
  AND a.value:"name"::STRING = '***TopName***'
  AND SUBSTR(CAST(p."publication_date" AS STRING),1,4) = '***BusiestYear***'
GROUP BY p."country_code"
ORDER BY patents_in_year_country DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9‑Same as #8 but showing only the top 5 jurisdiction codes.
SELECT 
       p."country_code"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc")      c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."assignee_harmonized") a
WHERE c.value:"symbol"::STRING ILIKE 'A61%'
  AND a.value:"name"::STRING = '***TopName***'
  AND SUBSTR(CAST(p."publication_date" AS STRING),1,4) = '***BusiestYear***'
GROUP BY p."country_code"
ORDER BY COUNT(DISTINCT p."publication_number") DESC
LIMIT 5;
```

```sql
--Description: 10‑Join with CPC_DEFINITION to fetch the textual title for A61 subgroup symbols.
SELECT 
       c.value:"symbol"::STRING      AS cpc_symbol,
       d."titleFull"                 AS cpc_title
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") c
LEFT JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.CPC_DEFINITION d
       ON d."symbol" = c.value:"symbol"::STRING
WHERE c.value:"symbol"::STRING ILIKE 'A61%'
LIMIT 20;
```
